          "exemptions": "Subdivision (e) exempts: transient and tourist hotel occupancy; housing in a nonprofit hospital, religious facility, extended care facility, licensed residential care facility for the elderly, or adult residential facility; dormitories owned and operated by a higher-education institution or K-12 school; tenants sharing bathroom or kitchen with an owner who lives on the property; single-family owner-occupied residences (renting no more than two units or bedrooms, or a mobilehome); two-unit single-structure properties where the owner occupied one unit at the start of the tenancy (neither unit an ADU or JADU); housing issued a certificate of occupancy within the previous 15 years (unless a mobilehome); separately alienable property whose owner is not a REIT, corporation, LLC with a corporate member, or mobilehome park management, and where the required written exemption notice was given; and deed- or regulation-restricted affordable housing or housing under a subsidy agreement.",
          "overrides": [],
          "interaction": "Section applies 'Notwithstanding any other law'. The text also cross-references the rent-limit statute (Civ. Code 1947.12) in the exemption notice, but that section is outside this chunk and was not extracted. Relocation assistance under (d)(3)(C) is credited against any other relocation assistance required by other law.",
          "effective_date": null,
          "source_doc_id": "D023",
          "conflict_flag": false,
          "conflict_note": null
        },
        {
          "team_rule_id": "r-62af20b103028b49",
          "jurisdiction": "CA",
          "level": "state",
          "category": "just_cause_eviction",
          "status": "in_force",
          "title": "Relocation assistance or final-month rent waiver for no-fault terminations",
          "requirement": "When an owner issues a termination notice based on no-fault just cause for a tenancy covered by the just cause requirement, the owner must, regardless of tenant income and at the owner's option, either pay relocation assistance or waive final-month rent in writing before it becomes due. The amount equals one month of the rent in effect when the notice was issued. Relocation assistance must be paid within 15 calendar days of service of the notice. The notice must tell the tenant of the right to relocation assistance or rent waiver, and if rent is waived, state the amount waived and that no rent is due for the final month. Failure to strictly comply voids the termination notice.",
          "citation": "Cal. Civ. Code § 1946.2(d)",
          "source_url": "https://leginfo.legislature.ca.gov/faces/codes_displaySection.xhtml?lawCode=CIV&sectionNum=1946.2",
          "quoted_span": "The amount of relocation assistance or rent waiver shall be equal to one month of the tenant’s rent that was in effect when the owner issued the notice to terminate the tenancy.",
          "key_value": "One month of rent; payment within 15 calendar days of service of notice",
          "coverage_conditions": {
