          "title": "Required contents of notice for demolition or substantial remodel terminations",
          "requirement": "A written termination notice based on intent to demolish or substantially remodel must state the owner's intent, include the statutory re-rent statement, describe the remodel (or expected demolition date) and expected duration, attach a copy of the required permit(s) (or, only for hazardous-material abatement needing no permit, a signed contractor contract), and notify the tenant to tell the owner of interest in reoccupying and provide address, phone, and email.",
          "citation": "Cal. Civ. Code § 1946.2(b)(2)(D)(iv)",
          "source_url": "https://leginfo.legislature.ca.gov/faces/codes_displaySection.xhtml?lawCode=CIV&sectionNum=1946.2",
